{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes","id":1415144,"title":"Scion with Kid Heroes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-22T18:38:39-07:00","id":1415144,"title":"Scion with Kid Heroes?","content":"I mentioned in the Once and Future thread that I watched last year's film The Kid Who Would Be King, which involved a group of 12 year old school kids being chosen as the spiritual inheritors of King Arthur and his knights, including possession of Excalibur. (It's a pretty good film and a fun watch; I recommend it if you have any interest in the subject matter or just enjoy good kids films.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, this led me to thinking about the idea of Scion games in which the PCs are, well, kids. Mainly those around 10 to 16, in Junior High or early High School (or their equivalent in other countries). So I'm soliciting thoughts and ideas about any rules alterations, genre shifts, Dial Adjustments, or the like that might be necessary or at least advisable for running such a game and/or making characters for it. <br /> <br /> (Obviously, some of the stuff I'm thinking about as possible inspiration for this sort of thing would be the first couple of Percy Jackson books, as well as its Egyptian and Norse spin offs, the Canadian Class of the Titans cartoon series from a few years ago, and perhaps stuff like Spirited Away or Natuto.) <br /> <br /> Any thoughts or ideas are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T18:58:46-07:00","id":1415147,"title":"","content":"I like this idea a lot.<br /> <br /> At first I was thinking on some reductions on how many dots a kid can have, as they are physically weaker and lack the experience on skills, but they are Heroes, so, they probably would follow the same rules as other characters.<br /> <br /> Still, I would suggest to avoid having more than 3 dots in any skill, and would keep physical as a secondary arena at most, dividing only in \u201cpopular\u201d (Social primary) and \u201cNerd\u201d (Mental primary), keeping the \u201cjocks\u201d as any one with secondary Physical and focus on Athletics and Close combat.<br /> <br /> For 10yo, maybe take the Role path away and the preferred approach, what reduce a lot the skills (-3 dots) and attributes (-3 dots). Later the character receives it when complete a certain age, maybe 12 and 15, I don\u2019t know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:02:10-07:00","id":1415148,"title":"","content":"Maybe Student/Kid would be the Role? Or a couple of different age appropriate ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:55:15-07:00","id":1415158,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about removing the role path to reduce the total skill dots to make the characters less experienced. But, it\u2019s not necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T19:58:00-07:00","id":1415159,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to represent a kid character is just with a condition of: \u201cKid\u201d which gives you Momentum for whenever adults don\u2019t take you seriously","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T20:02:05-07:00","id":1415160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415158#post1415158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about removing the role path to reduce the total skill dots to make the characters less experienced. But, it\u2019s not necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be interesting to have part of the story revolve around the kid characters discovering their role just as much as their callings as part of starting to establish their Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T20:04:51-07:00","id":1415162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415159#post1415159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best way to represent a kid character is just with a condition of: \u201cKid\u201d which gives you Momentum for whenever adults don\u2019t take you seriously</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that might be influenced by how the genre and evidence dials are set, I think. I'll have to get the Companion out and reread those parts with that in mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T01:29:06-07:00","id":1415169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415159#post1415159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best way to represent a kid character is just with a condition of: \u201cKid\u201d which gives you Momentum for whenever adults don\u2019t take you seriously</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this quite a bit. You see in a lot of books and movies where teenage protagonists seem to achieve things that adults never would, getting into much bigger scrapes and achieving greater and more long lasting victories. It would certainly represent a massive Momentum pool that the kid characters are drawing heavily on, because if they're gaining Momentum (to make up for the smaller skill and attribute pools) then they're getting it for <i>everything</i>.<br /> <br /> Bad guy runs into a night club. Kids can't get in. Momentum.<br /> Kids spotted carrying spears and swords and now they have to spend as much time avoiding the police and child services as fighting bad guys. Momentum.<br /> Need to catch a plane from Los Angeles to London without being stopped for being a possible runaway. Momentum.<br /> Need to hand over a large quantity of cash, or a card with the funds on it, for that plane ticket without people thinking you stole daddy's credit card. Momentum.<br /> Have to convince a police officer to run a plate of a possible Titan cultist? Good luck, kid. Momentum.<br /> <br /> I like this idea a <i>lot</i>. Especially when you mix it with removing the second Path and the Approach bonuses. The idea that the kid player picks up a couple of dice for their dice pool and, after just a few scenes where they're stacking on Momentum for the trials of being a kid, the player says 'Yeah and I'll totally add six Momentum dice to this.' like it's no thing, because they're drowning in that sweet Momentum is awesome.<br /> <br /> And watching them have to deal with that pool getting smaller as they age, and they have to rely more heavily on their emerging second Path and Approach (which is maybe doled out a few dots at a time over several stories) and to switch from channelling luck and enthusiasm to learning to lean on skill and power.<br /> <br /> There's nothing about this thread that I don't love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T04:56:59-07:00","id":1415179,"title":"","content":"I loved the way you put Momentum as enthusiasm going against the lack of experience.<br /> <br /> The smart kid may have a great plan, but what they don\u2019t know is adults have all kind of experiences and knows a lot of useless things. The kids try, try, they and suddenly \u201cbam\u201d, against all chances, they are victorious just because they believed they would.<br /> <br /> The idea of finding their role in society and finding the favorite way to approach problems was unintentional but makes sense on the psychological aspect, the kid is growing and discovering who he is going to be. They know where they come from and the family they are part of (pantheon), but all the rest is unknown, all they have is a bunch of basic knowledge and a few hobbies, the rest is pure luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T06:00:54-07:00","id":1415182,"title":"","content":"If you want to feature a difference in physical abilities you can simply use scale.<br /> Adjust the base scale 0 for the physical abilities of kids and adults get a scale 1in things like speed and power. (Not endurance tho, trust me on this :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T06:36:25-07:00","id":1415184,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'd do anything mechanically. There's no reason the 10 year old child of a god can't be as strong as an adult human, even pre-visitation, especially the child of a god with Epic Strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T07:17:02-07:00","id":1415189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415182#post1415182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to feature a difference in physical abilities you can simply use scale.<br /> Adjust the base scale 0 for the physical abilities of kids and adults get a scale 1in things like speed and power. (Not endurance tho, trust me on this :P)</div> </div> </div> </div>My 7yo can get tired quite fast, but he take just a minute to wind up again, while I can last longer, but once tired it takes me hours to be ok again.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a matter of scale, but maybe the Kid condition can increase difficulty in some might rolls (kids are pretty agile). I would not go that direction though, I really prefer to give the kids a lack of experience and not a lack of capacities, it\u2019s not that a kid is not as capable as an adult, it\u2019s that they didn\u2019t learn the tricks to use their strengths properly.<br /> <br /> I would make<br /> 10yo: lack favorite approach and role path<br /> 13yo: gains favorite approach<br /> 16yo: gains role path","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T16:04:06-07:00","id":1415335,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if age might also impact Callings. Such as being limited to only one dot at age 10 to 13 and to three dots at 13 to 16, again with part of the campaign usually focusing on the characters beginning to understand and grow into their future Callings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T17:02:18-07:00","id":1415341,"title":"","content":"Ehh I\u2019d say no, like I don\u2019t see any reason why a kid Scion would have less Callings dots, Scion Callings represent which mythical heroic and divine archetype you best fit in and has little to do with age or skill unless that\u2019s how the individual player decides to fluff their Knacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T17:13:50-07:00","id":1415342,"title":"","content":"I think maybe I'm thinking that kids age 10 to 13 might be a bit closer to Origin level than Hero, but it's just sort of a partially formed musing at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T17:20:38-07:00","id":1415343,"title":"","content":"Hercules and Khrisna both displayed super human strength as infants. Khrisna and Jesus performed miracles as five year olds. Bridgette gave away everything in her family's home to the poor but had more left when she was done than when she began, when she was seven. Hermes stole cattle and invented the harp and the flute all on the day of his birth. Artemis was born before her brother and then helped her mother with the delivery of her brother. Anubis, Cu chulain, Loki, and many others had adventures as infants and small children. So Scions ought to be powerful even as small children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T17:47:52-07:00","id":1415346,"title":"","content":"Counterpoint to &quot;Should younger Heroes have fewer Calling dots?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's magic. Who cares? Baby Krishna created infinite money and has the universe in his little baby mouth. It's myth. If you're playing a Visited Hero, give them their Hero powers. There's some Destructive Kid in Irish folklore who's so strong he needs to be wrangled by like... 27 grown men holding chains that are cuffed to the kid's body. And even then he still occasionally drags them around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-24-2020, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T18:24:18-07:00","id":1415348,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Good points. <br /> <br /> This may be one of those things where where the Myth Level dial is set might play a part, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T20:17:52-07:00","id":1415359,"title":"","content":"Sort of, yeah, discussion at the table and all that. Speaking personally if I were told that I was 1-2 Calling dots short because we were playing Camp Half-Blood I'd ask why being a kid meant we got less magic power, but that's a Me thing.<br /> <br /> I do like the &quot;You have a persistent condition of Kid and each time an adult doesn't take you seriously gain Momentum&quot; as an idea though. It allows for enriching the story in a fun way, IMO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T04:31:54-07:00","id":1415395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415359#post1415359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of, yeah, discussion at the table and all that. Speaking personally if I were told that I was 1-2 Calling dots short because we were playing Camp Half-Blood I'd ask why being a kid meant we got less magic power, but that's a Me thing.<br /> <br /> I do like the &quot;You have a persistent condition of Kid and each time an adult doesn't take you seriously gain Momentum&quot; as an idea though. It allows for enriching the story in a fun way, IMO</div> </div> </div> </div>You make some really good points.<br /> <br /> I love this whole idea!!! That would totally work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:30:49-07:00","id":1415600,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on having fewer Callings is simply a matter of experience is all. You're not 'less powerful because you're a kid' so much as you have had less experience and time in the world to have settled deeply into your calling/s. I mean ask any kid at age nine what they want to be and not too many will have strong convictions.<br /> <br /> Which is separate from power. Age doesn't necessarily prevent you from having as many Purviews as an adult. Heracles was already mightily...uh...mighty as a baby in his crib strangling snakes but I'd bet dollars to donuts that he had no idea what his <i>Callings</i> were.<br /> <br /> Also, IMHO you kind of have to be careful with comparisons of children in legend. There's a big difference between a child who was born to a mortal parent (or two) and a child who was born as an already-created-god. Hermes and Artemis (and others like them) were born gods and were in their full deific power right from the get go whereas many others were born part mortal and had to grow into their power. It's not necessarily the same playing field and not an accurate comparison.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:53:28-07:00","id":1415605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415600#post1415600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on having fewer Callings is simply a matter of experience is all. You're not 'less powerful because you're a kid' so much as you have had less experience and time in the world to have settled deeply into your calling/s. I mean ask any kid at age nine what they want to be and not too many will have strong convictions.<br /> <br /> Which is separate from power. Age doesn't necessarily prevent you from having as many Purviews as an adult. Heracles was already mightily...uh...mighty as a baby in his crib strangling snakes but I'd bet dollars to donuts that he had no idea what his <i>Callings</i> were.<br /> <br /> Also, IMHO you kind of have to be careful with comparisons of children in legend. There's a big difference between a child who was born to a mortal parent (or two) and a child who was born as an already-created-god. Hermes and Artemis (and others like them) were born gods and were in their full deific power right from the get go whereas many others were born part mortal and had to grow into their power. It's not necessarily the same playing field and not an accurate comparison.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part about Callings defo makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T17:45:18-07:00","id":1415628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415600#post1415600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on having fewer Callings is simply a matter of experience is all. You're not 'less powerful because you're a kid' so much as you have had less experience and time in the world to have settled deeply into your calling/s. I mean ask any kid at age nine what they want to be and not too many will have strong convictions.<br /> <br /> Which is separate from power. Age doesn't necessarily prevent you from having as many Purviews as an adult. Heracles was already mightily...uh...mighty as a baby in his crib strangling snakes but I'd bet dollars to donuts that he had no idea what his <i>Callings</i> were.<br /> <br /> Also, IMHO you kind of have to be careful with comparisons of children in legend. There's a big difference between a child who was born to a mortal parent (or two) and a child who was born as an already-created-god. Hermes and Artemis (and others like them) were born gods and were in their full deific power right from the get go whereas many others were born part mortal and had to grow into their power. It's not necessarily the same playing field and not an accurate comparison.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: Assuming you're a grown-ass adult at Origin, you have one (1) Calling Dot.<br /> <br /> Then you get your Visitation, and you suddenly jump to five (5) Calling Dots. All at once, gain 4 Calling Dots. At least two of them in Callings you didn't have BEFORE the Visitation.<br /> <br /> Would a Kid Character as an Origin Pre-Visitation Scion get <i>zero</i> Calling Dots and no Knacks because they're a kid?<br /> <br /> Experience doesn't have much to do with it. It doesn't make any sense to me.<br /> <br /> But granted, this is all abstraction. I bet nobody in-universe could name their Callings because Callings are an abstraction that I don't like to apply in-universe.<br /> <br /> Remember, CuChulainn was defending Ulster at what, 13? Tell me he had fewer Calling Dots. His Hero Tricks were fucking bonkers and the kid was using crazy numbers of Knacks.<br /> <br /> Classic myth didn't give a shit about if the Magic Hero was a kid or if they were an older adult. It's an arbitrary restriction. And I don't know about you, but I don't see many Scion games lasting long enough in-universe for the kids to not be kids anymore. So in practice you're locking away those extra Calling Dots and most players won't ever regain them.<br /> <br /> No, going &quot;You're a kid so you have fewer Calling dots&quot; is not a good mechanic. It restricts and punishes for wanting to be different, and what does it add? Fuck all. Making things worse for no reason is not good game design.<br /> <br /> Edit: When proposing a mechanic, ask yourself &quot;Does this make sense within the game?&quot; and &quot;Does this actually make the game better?&quot; The proposed &quot;Kids have fewer Calling dots because they're kids&quot; doesn't make sense because it applies some arbitrary restriction where there's no indication of it elsewhere, and it doesn't actually improve the game in my mind, because it's telling me to be less effective Just Because, and no I don't get anything to compensate, and you're basically going to be hobbled for most game lengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-26-2020, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T18:21:45-07:00","id":1415635,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I feel that a key part of the kid genre - or maybe at least one of the potential focuses for such a game, I guess - is self discovery, including figuring out who you are and what you want to be. Including the &quot;oh, cool! I can do<i> that</i> now!&quot; moment of discovering new powers. On the other hand, I can certainly see the appeal of just starting with &quot;we are the most awesome kids to have ever awesomed!&quot; and just running with it. <br /> <br /> But I admit that I also have this tendency to want to have the transition from Origin to Hero be played out similarly to the way the transition from Hero to Demigod would be. At least if I were going to start at Origin level. If I were starting a game at Hero level, I'd just have that be blue-booked/included in prelude and/or character backstory. <br /> <br /> I think maybe the issue of Callings comes down to the question of Are these kid characters just now emerging into the world of Heroes or are they already Heroes? If the former, these I think maybe it might be appropriate to have at least the first story arc involve the characters coming into their new Callings. But if the latter, then they already have them all. <br /> <br /> So, in this context, I think the Callings would depend on how everyone agreed they wanted to start the game out. <br /> <br /> But that things like not having a Favored Approach and/or Role at certain ages, as well as gaining Momentum when adults don't take you seriously because you're &quot;just a kid&quot; are probably ideas that would work well regardless of if the character is already a Hero or not. (Maybe even for Demigods? I have no idea about that one.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T18:35:35-07:00","id":1415642,"title":"","content":"Hm, now if you had some Origin kids... And then picked a couple Adoption Deeds to pick the OTHER Callings that they'll get come their Visitation, that could be a fun game. Maybe punctuate it by saying that you can pick Knacks for any of your declared Callings, but can only have one Heroic Knack active at a time, it'd allow for some more variety and represent the expanding powers.<br /> <br /> Actually that'd probably be a fun way to ease from Origin to Hero for most games. I'll keep that in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-26-2020, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T20:21:26-07:00","id":1415647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415628#post1415628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Counterpoint: Assuming you're a grown-ass adult at Origin, you have one (1) Calling Dot.<br /> <br /> Then you get your Visitation, and you suddenly jump to five (5) Calling Dots. All at once, gain 4 Calling Dots. At least two of them in Callings you didn't have BEFORE the Visitation.<br /> <br /> Would a Kid Character as an Origin Pre-Visitation Scion get <i>zero</i> Calling Dots and no Knacks because they're a kid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Countercounterpoint <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd argue that those extra Calling dots are an adult sinking deeper into the experiences that they've had, in effect 'fleshing out' who they already are. They haven't magically gained extra stuff so much as expanded what they already were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415628#post1415628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Experience doesn't have much to do with it. It doesn't make any sense to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is totally fair. Your game, your rules and, as below...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415628#post1415628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But granted, this is all abstraction. I bet nobody in-universe could name their Callings because Callings are an abstraction that I don't like to apply in-universe.<br /> <br /> Remember, CuChulainn was defending Ulster at what, 13? Tell me he had fewer Calling Dots. His Hero Tricks were fucking bonkers and the kid was using crazy numbers of Knacks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. It's hard to use a game system to represent 'real life examples'. There are always going to be exceptions or things that don't fit. I don't know much of anything about Cu Chulainn so I couldnt' comment, but you seem to and I'm more than happy to bow to your greater knowledge there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415628#post1415628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Classic myth didn't give a shit about if the Magic Hero was a kid or if they were an older adult. It's an arbitrary restriction. And I don't know about you, but I don't see many Scion games lasting long enough in-universe for the kids to not be kids anymore. So in practice you're locking away those extra Calling Dots and most players won't ever regain them.<br /> <br /> No, going &quot;You're a kid so you have fewer Calling dots&quot; is not a good mechanic. It restricts and punishes for wanting to be different, and what does it add? Fuck all. Making things worse for no reason is not good game design.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. Although from my view 'locking away' and 'punishing' aren't exactly the words I would use. Not having something because you wouldn't have them isn't a punishment. A real fourteen year old, for example, isn't being punished when they're not able to have a drivers licence or to buy beer (your mileage may vary, because beer is awesome). They're simply considered too young to be allowed to. Nobody is discriminating against them, so much as recognising that they don't have the experience or maturity to safely do so. It's simply widely recognised that children don't have the same knowledge and capacity to achieve or do certain things as an adult does.<br /> <br /> Again, though, if in your game or in your opinion it's the other, then so be it. If it fits the narrative of your game or your character idea that a juvenile scion has everything that an adult one would then that's cool. I dare say most of us would run the same given thing (whether it relates to age or any other subject) differently. If it's fun for you and your players then that's probably the right way to call it. There are certainly exceptions in the real world now, of young people who are uncommonly wise and together and plenty of examples of adults who aren't. Play your game how ever it fits your world view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415628#post1415628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: When proposing a mechanic, ask yourself &quot;Does this make sense within the game?&quot; and &quot;Does this actually make the game better?&quot; The proposed &quot;Kids have fewer Calling dots because they're kids&quot; doesn't make sense because it applies some arbitrary restriction where there's no indication of it elsewhere, and it doesn't actually improve the game in my mind, because it's telling me to be less effective Just Because, and no I don't get anything to compensate, and you're basically going to be hobbled for most game lengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, fair points and obviously true at your table. Respect. Although along side all the things that kids are kept out of, they do get certain things that may be viewed as compensation from the narrative viewpoint. They can get away with a lot of things an adult couldn't. Adults, as a whole, are often taught to think of them as 'good kids' and in need of guidance or education rather than the stern punishment an adult doing the same thing may face. Children tend to elicit a sympathy and empathy that adults may not, and to set off an adult's protective urges. When your thirteen year old scion is send running along by a police officer, being told &quot;And don't let me catch you doing this again! Don't make me drag your folks in!&quot; rather than being arrested or charged they've scored a free pass that an adult would need to use a knack or other power for.<br /> <br /> Overall I respect your viewpoint and I appreciate the debate. You've made some valid points that I'll have to think on. Thank you for the response <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T20:49:51-07:00","id":1415651,"title":"","content":"Happy to help. Sorry if I came across as aggressive there, I can sound a lot harsher than I intend sometimes.<br /> <br /> Also I literally never accept &quot;But realistically-&quot; for a game, especially not for a game like Scion. Like, this is a game where I can play a talking dog that can headbutt a bus across a city block before howling and releasing a firestorm. This game isn't even trying to adhere to anything like 'Modern ideas of realistic restraint'. Feels kind of silly to try and cite it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T04:52:41-07:00","id":1415673,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> wow. Idk that about Cu Chulainn. That\u2019s really cool. I guess there\u2019s no reason teen (or younger) Scions couldn\u2019t be full-fledged Heroes. There\u2019s lots of examples in modern superhero myth (Teen Titans, X-Men).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2608_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2608\" data-vbnamecard=\"2608\">Squee</a> true, but to the kid or teen it defo feels like punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-27-2020, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T11:34:07-07:00","id":1415861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415673#post1415673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> wow. Idk that about Cu Chulainn. That\u2019s really cool. I guess there\u2019s no reason teen (or younger) Scions couldn\u2019t be full-fledged Heroes. There\u2019s lots of examples in modern superhero myth (Teen Titans, X-Men).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not super familiar with the Tain, but I know some tidbits.<br /> <br /> Like for instance, a lot of modern tellings of the story of CuChulainn put his death there, at the defense of Ulster. But in classical sources, he survives, the battle is mostly futile, and then he gets a good taste of the consequences of his own actions in &quot;The Death of Chulainn&quot;, when he's like middle aged and the families of all the people he's killed decide &quot;Hey fuck this guy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Apparently some people thought &quot;13 year old dies fighting the Good Fight defending his home&quot; made a better story and that telling caught on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-28-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T13:15:28-07:00","id":1415877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415144-scion-with-kid-heroes?p=1415861#post1415861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not super familiar with the Tain, but I know some tidbits.<br /> <br /> Like for instance, a lot of modern tellings of the story of CuChulainn put his death there, at the defense of Ulster. But in classical sources, he survives, the battle is mostly futile, and then he gets a good taste of the consequences of his own actions in &amp;quot;The Death of Chulainn&amp;quot;, when he's like middle aged and the family of all the people he's killed decide &amp;quot;Hey fuck this guy&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Apparently some people thought &amp;quot;13 year old dies fighting the Good Fight defending his home&amp;quot; made a better story and that telling caught on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating. Thank you.<br /> <br /> That is a pretty cool story. Do you think Cu Chulainn reached Apotheosis? Or is that a definite No?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T13:41:18-07:00","id":1415882,"title":"","content":"I think CuChulainn is going to be statted as a Demigod Who Didn't Quite Make It in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T15:09:44-07:00","id":1415891,"title":"","content":"Perfect! I haven\u2019t gotten that far in the Kickstarter yet. Looking forward to it \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}